From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] shell: let the visible stack page own keyboard focus

Whichever page is showing has to own focus, or key events stop at the window
and never reach that page's own controllers. Two workflows were broken by
this: an embedded Activity never saw a keystroke, because the Casilda
compositor was not the event target; and Home never ran its type-to-search,
because HomeWindow was not on the propagation path.

Nothing on the Activity page can take focus by itself - the Activity is a
separate Wayland client, opaque to this process's focus chain - and a
finishing stack transition recomputes focus and drops it again, so a grab
issued at switch time does not survive. Claim focus for the visible page
when it becomes visible and again once a transition settles.

Sugar's F1-F8 capture is unaffected: those controllers sit on the window,
the overlay and the stack, all ancestors of both pages, so capture phase
still reaches them first.
--- a/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/model/shell.py
@@ -425,6 +425,14 @@
         self._main_window = None
 
         self.compositor = Casilda.Compositor(socket="wayland-sugar")
+        # An embedded Activity only receives Wayland key events while the
+        # compositor is the window's focus widget. Nothing else on that stack
+        # page can take focus, and a finishing stack transition recomputes
+        # focus, so claim it whenever the page becomes or settles as visible.
+        self.stack.connect('notify::visible-child',
+                           self._stack_focus_cb)
+        self.stack.connect('notify::transition-running',
+                           self._stack_focus_cb)
 
         self.connect('window-added', self._window_added_cb)
         self.connect('window-removed', self._window_removed_cb)
@@ -514,6 +522,7 @@
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("journal")
             else:
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("activity")
+                self._focus_compositor()
         else:
             self.stack.set_visible_child_name("home")
 
@@ -523,6 +532,27 @@
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("journal")
             else:
                 self.stack.set_visible_child_name("activity")
+                self._focus_compositor()
+
+    def _focus_compositor(self):
+        GLib.idle_add(self._grab_compositor_focus)
+
+    def _stack_focus_cb(self, stack, _param):
+        if not stack.get_transition_running():
+            GLib.idle_add(self._grab_compositor_focus)
+
+    def _grab_compositor_focus(self):
+        # Whichever page is showing has to own focus, or key events stop at
+        # the window and never reach the page's own controllers: the Activity
+        # never sees a keystroke, and Home never runs its type-to-search.
+        name = self.stack.get_visible_child_name()
+        if name == 'activity':
+            self.compositor.grab_focus()
+        elif name == 'home':
+            page = self.stack.get_child_by_name('home')
+            if page is not None:
+                page.grab_focus()
+        return False
 
     def _get_activities_with_window(self):
         ret = []
